# OxideOS Ubuntu LiveFS Prototype Experiment

## Project

OxideOS - RedWolf Studios

## Prototype

OxideOS-test4.iso

## Date

October 2026

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Objective

This experiment tested whether Ubuntu could serve as a foundation for an
early OxideOS prototype.

Goals:

-   Modify an Ubuntu live ISO
-   Edit the live filesystem
-   Add LXQt desktop environment
-   Add SDDM display manager
-   Create a bootable custom ISO
-   Verify a graphical desktop session

This was a proof-of-concept build, not the final OxideOS release.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Background

Previous Fedora research explored Lorax and livemedia-creator.

The Fedora build successfully produced a live ISO, but the installer
environment failed due to missing Anaconda runtime dependencies.

The project moved to Ubuntu to investigate a different live image
workflow.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ubuntu LiveFS Research

Ubuntu uses:

-   Casper live boot system
-   SquashFS filesystem
-   initrd boot scripts
-   live user creation
-   desktop session configuration

Important discovery:

A live ISO and an installed system are separate layers.

A working live environment does not automatically mean the installer
will install the modified environment.

